Enhancement: Add `backup --exclude-older-than` and `--exclude-newer-than` options

The `backup` command can now exclude files based on their modification time.
Both options accept either an age relative to the backup time (`--time`, or
now by default), such as `30d` or `1y2m`, or an absolute time, such as
`2024-01-31` or `2024-01-31 12:00`.

For example, `restic backup ~/work --exclude-older-than 1y` only backs up files
modified within the last year.

